            <ArticleTitle>Giant cecal diverticulum in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e23-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2011.03.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old girl with abdominal pain and fever underwent urgent surgery. As was suspected on computed tomographic scan, a large diverticular mass adherent to the cecum was identified. A diverticulectomy was performed. We report this rare case of a giant cecal diverticulum and provide an overview of known literature.</AbstractText>
